Evidence 3: clean compile + link of the dialect lib and opt tool under C++20
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[3/6] Building CXX object lib/IR/CMakeFiles/obj.MLIRPolyKernel.dir/__/__/include/PolyKernel/IR/PolyKernelDialect.cpp.o
[4/6] Linking CXX static library lib/libMLIRPolyKernel.a
[5/6] Building CXX object tools/polykernel-opt/CMakeFiles/polykernel-opt.dir/polykernel-opt.cpp.o
[6/6] Linking CXX executable tools/polykernel-opt/polykernel-opt
BUILD_EXIT=0

Compiler: clang++ 21.1.8 (llvmPackages_21.clang), matching MLIR-21 headers.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Fallback path (NOT taken, documented for the record)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Had MLIR-21 headers rejected C++20, the plan was to set CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 17
project-wide and rebuild green (the upstream mlir/examples/standalone defaults
to C++17). This was unnecessary: MLIR 21.1.8 headers compile cleanly under
-std=c++20 with llvmPackages_21.clang.

Chosen standard for PolyKernel going forward: C++20.
